{
  "description": "Source downloads for the statically linked copyleft (LGPL/GPL) components, published in each release's runai-model-streamer-sources-X.Y.Z.tar.gz (built by .github/scripts/release_sources.py). Add an entry when a component linked statically into the native libraries has a copyleft licence in cpp/NOTICE without a runtime exception such as GCC-exception-3.1. id is the component's name in cpp/NOTICE (its last path segment); dir is its folder in the archive; files lists each upstream source file with its url and sha256. Use a url that keeps old versions (Launchpad's +sourcefiles for Ubuntu packages, not the archive pool, which drops a version when a newer update is published).Change an entry together with the version that cpp/NOTICE shows for the component: the release build fails when an id has no row in cpp/NOTICE or the versions differ. registry lists the files that the Bazel Central Registry holds for a module the build takes from it (source.json and the overlay build files), published under build-materials/bazel-registry/ because the libraries cannot be rebuilt without them: add an entry for each statically linked module that the registry builds, with the version cpp/MODULE.bazel depends on (the release build fails when they differ), and update its files and sha256 when that version changes.",
